# ************************************
#   Comments + Keyword Clarification

#    Anton, Calculus, 0.1.9a
# ************************************
# DESCRIPTION
# Determine the domain and range of f(x) = B/x-A

# ENDDESCRIPTION
## DBsubject('Calculus')
## DBchapter('Before Calculus')
## DBsection('Functions')
## KEYWORDS('Functions', 'Domain', 'Range')
## TitleText1('Calculus')
## EditionText1('9')
## AuthorText1('Anton')
## Section1('0.1')
## Problem1('9a')
## Author('')
## Institution('John Wiley & Sons')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric");
#****************************************************
#  Create function of form A/(x - B)
#****************************************************
$A    = non_zero_random(-9, 9);
$B    = non_zero_random(-9, 9);
$Func = Formula("$A/(x - $B)")->reduce;
#**************
#   Answers
#**************
Context("Interval");
$Domain = Compute("(-inf,$B) U ($B,inf)");
$Range  = Compute("(-inf,0) U (0,inf)");
#*******************
#   Display stuff
#*******************
Context("Numeric")->variables->add(y => 'Real');
$XofY = Formula("($A + $B y)/y")->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML
Find the domain and range of the function [``f(x) = [$Func] ``]. Express each in
interval notation.

a) Domain: [_]{$Domain}

b) Range: [_]{$Range}

[@ helpLink('interval') @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
For a rational function such as [``f(x) =[$Func] ``], the domain is restricted to
all values of [`x`] that do not produce a zero in the denominator.

For this function, the domain may include all real values of [`x`] except for 
[`x = [$B]`]. In interval notation, this is [`[$Domain]`].

To determine the range of this function, note that since the numerator is fixed at [$A] the function 
can never equal 0. Alternatively, if you solve this equation for [`x`] in terms of
[`y`],
[```
\begin{aligned}
y & = [$Func]\\
y(x - [$B]) &= [$A]\\
yx - [$B] y &= [$A]\\
yx & = [$B]y + [$A] \\
x &=[$XofY]
\end{aligned}```]
It is now evident that [`y = 0`] is not in the range of the function. Expressed using
interval notation, this is [`[$Range]`].

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
